## 1. FIX PASS (do this first; these are confirmed bugs)
==================================================
F1. SLANT/TRANSFORM CONFLICT. `.df-slant-block { transform: skewX(...) }` is overridden by `.df-interactive:hover/:focus-visible/:active { transform: translate3d(...) }`, which makes every slanted chip, tab and node un-skew and jump on hover (ModelComparison tabs, PracticeConstellation chips and hub, HospitalityEcosystem chips, GrowthMarketingPage chips). FIX: use the INDIVIDUAL transform properties for hover motion (`translate: 0 var(--lift)`, `scale: 0.985`, never the `transform` shorthand) so they compose with the skew. Add `translate`/`scale` to the `transition-property` lists. Verify visually that slanted elements keep their slant before, during and after hover.

F2. REDUCED MOTION KILLS ALL FEEDBACK. The current `prefers-reduced-motion` block removes every hover transform and hides `.df-ambient::after` entirely, leaving no visible feedback. FIX with tiers (spec in 2.6): under reduced motion keep colour, border-illumination, glow and shadow changes (static, no movement); remove only translate/scale/tilt/zoom/sweeps/autoplay.

F3. MEDIA QUERY TOO STRICT. Replace `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` with `(any-hover: hover) and (any-pointer: fine)` for hover styles so hybrid laptops and emulators work. Keep the `(hover: none)` / coarse-pointer press behavior for touch.

F4. TIER-2 (.df-ambient) IS EFFECTIVELY INVISIBLE (a 7.5%-opacity static gradient that only fades in). About 28 blocks use it, so most of the site feels dead. FIX: redesign it so it is clearly perceptible but never looks like a button:
- on hover/focus-within: border changes to an illuminated hairline gradient (violet→magenta at 45–60% opacity in Night, 35% in Day) via a masked pseudo-element (same technique as `.df-interactive::before`);
- a soft light band (about 12–16% opacity, slanted at `--slant`) that TRAVELS across the block once over about 900ms (animate `translate`, not opacity-only);
- the card's eyebrow/number text brightens one step; nothing scales, cursor stays `default`, no arrows;
- lift at most 2px via `translate`.

F5. SERVICES COLOUR MISMATCH + SITEWIDE CARD CONSISTENCY. In `ServicesPage.tsx` the "Architecture Overview" row mixes a permanently dark `df-mesh-dark` card (raw `text-[var(--magenta)]` label) with two `df-card-surface` cards (labels using `--link-accent` and `--eyebrow-magenta`), so the three blocks look like three different materials and change differently between Day and Night. FIX:
- One material for sibling cards: all three use the same surface class and the same label style. Express emphasis (the "Core" card) with an accent rim/top-edge (2px violet→magenta gradient) and a slanted marker colour (violet = core, blue = acts, magenta = shows up), NOT a different background.
- One label token: use a single `Eyebrow`-style class for all small uppercase labels. Replace raw `text-[var(--magenta)]` on light surfaces with `--eyebrow-magenta`, and `--link-accent` for labels with `--eyebrow-blue`. Keep raw magenta only on genuinely dark panels.
- Audit the same pattern elsewhere and fix it the same way: `ReportingVsIntelligence.tsx:38`, `ModelComparison.tsx:60`, `DigitalTransformationPage.tsx:98`, `HospitalityPage.tsx:130`, `MegaMenu.tsx:80`, `PracticeConstellation.tsx:144`. A dark panel is acceptable as a deliberate FEATURE block (one per grid, larger or spanning), but never as one of several equal siblings. If a grid has mixed materials, unify them. Day and Night must both look consistent (check both).

F6. SERVICES DIRECTORY ROWS ARE INERT. The "Practice Directory" `<article>` rows have no hover class and only a small button is interactive. Apply the row interaction defined in Section 5.

